1
00:00:00,396 --> 00:00:03,236
An eight-day supply
of food and water, a crossbow...

2
00:00:03,399 --> 00:00:05,859
...season two of
Star Trek: The Original Series...

3
00:00:06,027 --> 00:00:07,697
...on a high-density flash drive.

4
00:00:08,821 --> 00:00:11,661
(Elizabeth:)What if there's a disaster
that destroys all the USB ports?

5
00:00:12,283 --> 00:00:14,623
(Sheldon:)Then there's really
no reason to live, is there?

6
00:00:14,827 --> 00:00:17,327
(Elizabeth:)Can I ask you a question
about your roommate?

7
00:00:17,539 --> 00:00:20,119
(Sheldon:)He's an odd duck, isn't he?

8
00:00:20,625 --> 00:00:22,335
(Elizabeth:)What's his relationship status?

9
00:00:22,544 --> 00:00:25,214
(Sheldon:)Well, there was
a misbegotten adventure...

10
00:00:25,380 --> 00:00:27,550
(Sheldon:)...with a waitress
who lives across the hall.

11
00:00:27,715 --> 00:00:29,805
(Sheldon:)It ended as inexplicably as it began.

12
00:00:30,009 --> 00:00:33,259
(Sheldon:)They had very little in common
except for carnal activity.

13
00:00:33,471 --> 00:00:36,851
(Sheldon:)That's why I acquired
these noise-canceling headphones.

14
00:00:37,058 --> 00:00:40,348
(Sheldon:)If you decide to use them,
please clean the earpieces afterwards...

15
00:00:40,520 --> 00:00:42,900
(Sheldon:)...with the Wet Wipes
you'll find in the bathroom.

16
00:00:43,064 --> 00:00:45,064
(Sheldon:)They're in the drawer
labeled "Wet Wipes."

17
00:00:45,650 --> 00:00:46,820
(Leonard:)-Okay.
-Good.

18
00:00:46,985 --> 00:00:49,155
(Sheldon:)I'll leave you
to your nighttime ablutions.

19
00:00:49,320 --> 00:00:51,610
(Sheldon:)I've e-mailed you
the morning bathroom schedule.

20
00:00:51,781 --> 00:00:55,161
(Sheldon:)You'll also find a laminated copy
in your welcome packet.

21
00:00:57,078 --> 00:00:59,618
(Sheldon:)On the back of
the emergency-escape-route diagram.

22
00:00:59,831 --> 00:01:01,021
(Elizabeth:)How thoughtful.

